`,e.jsxs(s.p,{children:[e.jsx(s.strong,{children:"Stage offload."})," Consider two sequential single-replica stages on one GPU, of which only one keeps its weights on the GPU at a time. When execution switches from the first stage to the second, the first stage's weights are unloaded to host memory after it completes, and the second stage's weights are loaded before it runs. Only weight residency changes; the topology and the request binding stay fixed. KV caches remain on the GPU and continue to count toward the memory budget."]}),`
